      "source": [
        "**Rationale for Data Cleaning Decisions**\n",
        "To ensure the integrity and relevance of our analysis, i made the following data cleaning decisions:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dropping Columns with High Missing Values:** Columns such as RETURN_DATE, PAYMENT_AMOUNT, and ADJUSTMENT_AMOUNT were removed from the DataFrame. These columns contained a significant number of missing values, which, if retained, could introduce bias or reduce the reliability of our analysis. Removing them helps us focus on more complete and actionable data points.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Forward-Filling Missing Dates: For date-related columns**, including TOTAL_DUE_TODAY, BALANCE_DUE_TO_DATE, BALANCE, and MAX_PAYMENT_DATE, missing values were filled using the forward-fill (ffill) method. This approach assumes that the last observed valid value is carried forward to fill subsequent missing entries, which is a common and appropriate technique for time-series data where values tend to persist or follow a sequential pattern over short periods. This ensures continuity in our time-based analysis.\n"
      ]
    },
