      "source": [
        "**Here are the problems found in the data and how to fix them:**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **What’s wrong with the data?**\n",
        " a)The **\"Paid Off\"** Mistake: Many accounts are marked as \"Paid Off,\" but the data shows they still owe money. This is confusing and makes the portfolio look healthier than it actually is.\n",
        "\n",
        " b)**Missing People Info**: We have \"Loan IDs\" but not \"Customer IDs.\" We don't know if one person has three bad loans under different numbers.\n",
        "\n",
        "c)**Math Errors:** In some cases, the \"Total Paid\" amount actually went down over time. Unless money was refunded, this means the numbers were typed in wrong.\n",
        "\n",
        "d)**Missing Income:** We don't know how much many customers earn, so we can't tell if we are lending too much to people who can't afford it.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**2. How to fix it**\n",
        "To make tracking easier, MoPhones should do these three things:\n",
        "\n",
        "**A. Create a \"Customer ID\"**\n",
        "Give every person one unique ID. This way, if they fail to pay for one phone, the system knows not to give them another one.\n",
        "\n",
        "**B. Auto-Update Status**\n",
        "The system should only mark a loan as \"Paid Off\" when the balance hits zero. No more manual clicking. This keeps the data honest.\n",
        "\n",
        "**C. Use \"Reason Codes\"**\n",
        "When a payment is adjusted or skipped, the staff should pick a reason from a list (like \"Late Fee Waived\" or \"Phone Stolen\"). This helps the CCO understand why money is being lost.\n",
        "\n",
        " *\"The data is good, but it's messy. By automating your status updates and linking loans to specific people, we can stop losing money to simple human errors.\"*"
      ]
